{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BinaryInteger"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s23CustomStringConvertibleP","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/CustomStringConvertible","text":"CustomStringConvertible"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Hashable","text":"Hashable"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sj","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Numeric","text":"Numeric"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sx","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Strideable","text":"Strideable"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sj9MagnitudeQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Numeric\/Magnitude-swift.associatedtype","text":"Magnitude"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sz","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger","text":"BinaryInteger"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sj9MagnitudeQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Numeric\/Magnitude-swift.associatedtype","text":"Magnitude"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sj9MagnitudeQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Numeric\/Magnitude-swift.associatedtype","text":"Magnitude"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"text":"Magnitude","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/Numeric\/Magnitude-swift.associatedtype","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sj9MagnitudeQa"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryInteger"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol is the basis for all the integer types"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"provided by the standard library. All of the standard library’s integer"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"types, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UInt32"},{"type":"text","text":", conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryInteger"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":1,"text":"Converting Between Numeric Types","anchor":"Converting-Between-Numeric-Types","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can create new instances of a type that conforms to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryInteger","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol from a floating-point number or another binary integer of any","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"BinaryInteger","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol provides initializers for four","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"different kinds of conversion.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Range-Checked-Conversion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Range-Checked Conversion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You use the default ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" initializer to create a new instance when","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"you’re sure that the value passed is representable in the new type. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, an instance of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int16","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" can represent the value ","type":"text"},{"code":"500","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"first conversion in the code sample below succeeds. That same value is too","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"large to represent as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Int8","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instance, so the second conversion fails,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"triggering a runtime error.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let x: Int = 500","let y = Int16(x)","\/\/ y == 500","","let z = Int8(x)","\/\/ Error: Not enough bits to represent..."]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When you create a binary integer from a floating-point value using the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"default initializer, the value is rounded toward zero before the range is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"checked. In the following example, the value "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"127.75"},{"type":"text","text":" is rounded to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"127"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which is representable by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int8"},{"text":" type.  ","type":"text"},{"code":"128.25","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is rounded to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"128"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"which is not representable as an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int8"},{"text":" instance, triggering a runtime","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"error."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let e = Int8(127.75)","\/\/ e == 127","","let f = Int8(128.25)","\/\/ Error: Double value cannot be converted..."]},{"anchor":"Exact-Conversion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Exact Conversion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init?(exactly:)"},{"type":"text","text":" initializer to create a new instance after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checking whether the passed value is representable. Instead of trapping on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out-of-range values, using the failable "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init?(exactly:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"initializer results in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let x = Int16(exactly: 500)","\/\/ x == Optional(500)","","let y = Int8(exactly: 500)","\/\/ y == nil"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When converting floating-point values, the ","type":"text"},{"code":"init?(exactly:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" initializer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checks both that the passed value has no fractional part and that the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value is representable in the resulting type.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let e = Int8(exactly: 23.0)       \/\/ integral value, representable","\/\/ e == Optional(23)","","let f = Int8(exactly: 23.75)      \/\/ fractional value, representable","\/\/ f == nil","","let g = Int8(exactly: 500.0)      \/\/ integral value, nonrepresentable","\/\/ g == nil"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Clamping Conversion","anchor":"Clamping-Conversion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(clamping:)"},{"text":" initializer to create a new instance of a binary","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integer type where out-of-range values are clamped to the representable","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range of the type. For a type ","type":"text"},{"code":"T","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the resulting value is in the range","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"T.min...T.max"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let x = Int16(clamping: 500)","\/\/ x == 500","","let y = Int8(clamping: 500)","\/\/ y == 127","","let z = UInt8(clamping: -500)","\/\/ z == 0"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Bit-Pattern-Conversion","text":"Bit Pattern Conversion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use the "},{"code":"init(truncatingIfNeeded:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" initializer to create a new instance"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"with the same bit pattern as the passed value, extending or truncating the"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value’s representation as necessary. Note that the value may not be","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"preserved, particularly when converting between signed to unsigned integer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"types or when the destination type has a smaller bit width than the source","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"type. The following example shows how extending and truncating work for"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"nonnegative integers:"}]},{"code":["let q: Int16 = 850","\/\/ q == 0b00000011_01010010","","let r = Int8(truncatingIfNeeded: q)      \/\/ truncate 'q' to fit in 8 bits","\/\/ r == 82","\/\/   == 0b01010010","","let s = Int16(truncatingIfNeeded: r)     \/\/ extend 'r' to fill 16 bits","\/\/ s == 82","\/\/   == 0b00000000_01010010"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Any padding is performed by ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"sign-extending"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" the passed value. When"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"nonnegative integers are extended, the result is padded with zeroes. When"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"negative integers are extended, the result is padded with ones. This"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example shows several extending conversions of a negative value—note","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that negative values are sign-extended even when converting to an unsigned","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"type.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let t: Int8 = -100","\/\/ t == -100","\/\/ t's binary representation == 0b10011100","","let u = UInt8(truncatingIfNeeded: t)","\/\/ u == 156","\/\/ u's binary representation == 0b10011100","","let v = Int16(truncatingIfNeeded: t)","\/\/ v == -100","\/\/ v's binary representation == 0b11111111_10011100","","let w = UInt16(truncatingIfNeeded: t)","\/\/ w == 65436","\/\/ w's binary representation == 0b11111111_10011100"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":1,"anchor":"Comparing-Across-Integer-Types","type":"heading","text":"Comparing Across Integer Types"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can use relational operators, such as the less-than and equal-to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operators (","type":"text"},{"code":"<","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"==","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), to compare instances of different binary integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"types. The following example compares instances of the "},{"code":"Int","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"UInt","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"UInt8","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" types:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let x: Int = -23","let y: UInt = 1_000","let z: UInt8 = 23","","if x < y {","    print(\"\\(x) is less than \\(y).\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"-23 is less than 1000.\"","","if z > x {","    print(\"\\(z) is greater than \\(x).\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"23 is greater than -23.\""],"syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/binaryinteger"]}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/init()"],"anchor":"Creating-a-Binary-Integer","title":"Creating a Binary Integer"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/init(_:)-8gmdl","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/init(clamping:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/init(truncatingIfNeeded:)"],"anchor":"Converting-Integers","title":"Converting Integers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/init(_:)-2ln0u"],"anchor":"Converting-Floating-Point-Values","title":"Converting Floating-Point Values"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/init(exactly:)"],"anchor":"Converting-with-No-Loss-of-Precision","title":"Converting with No Loss of Precision"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/binary-integer-operators","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/quotientAndRemainder(dividingBy:)","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/isMultiple(of:)"],"anchor":"Performing-Calculations","title":"Performing Calculations"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/signum()"],"anchor":"Finding-the-Sign-and-Magnitude","title":"Finding the Sign and Magnitude"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/isSigned"],"anchor":"Accessing-Numeric-Constants","title":"Accessing Numeric Constants"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/BinaryInteger\/bitWidth","doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/B